# NOT CONVERGED

Static review found two blocker-level evasions. No generated-input tests or new documents were created.

### SOL-R6-01 — escaped/newline variants bypass refusal

- **Location:** [vertex_mutation.py:331](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/lang/src/lang/vertex_mutation.py:331)
- **Severity:** blocker
- **Claim:** The scan does not refuse every parser-supported newline-spanning quoted string.

When a backslash precedes LF, `esc` is cleared at lines 335–336 before the newline check at line 341, so the newline is accepted. KDL explicitly permits backslash-plus-literal-whitespace, including newlines, as a whitespace escape. KDL also defines newline characters beyond LF—CR, NEL, VT, FF, LS, and PS—while the code checks only `"\n"`. [Official KDL specification](https://kdl.dev/spec/)

Static completion path:

1. The domain guard accepts the escaped newline.
2. `kdl_find_block` uses `splitlines()` and counts braces without string awareness at [population.py:420](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/lang/src/lang/population.py:420).
3. Braces following the escaped newline are string data to ckdl but structure to the splice scanner.
4. The false block boundary can hide a duplicate sibling from `_assert_unique_kind_nodes`.
5. `remove_vertex_kind` can delete the target span plus a same-line sibling.
6. A later identical duplicate survives, so `_verified` observes the expected parsed mapping and accepts the mutation.

**Fix direction:** recognize the complete KDL newline set and refuse it before escape-state handling, regardless of whether the newline participates in a whitespace escape.

### SOL-R6-02 — block-comment quotes can conceal `r"` openers

- **Location:** [vertex_mutation.py:331](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/lang/src/lang/vertex_mutation.py:331)
- **Severity:** blocker
- **Claim:** The position-aware `r"` rule assumes every `"` encountered is string syntax, but quotes inside block comments have no string meaning.

A same-line block comment containing one quote sets `in_str=True`. A following zero-hash raw opener is consequently treated as a closing plain-string quote, bypassing the `prev == "r"` check. The raw closing quote reverses the state, and another one-quote block comment can rebalance it before newline/EOF. Neither the hashed/triple substring guards nor the unterminated-string check fires. KDL block comments may contain such quote characters. [Official KDL specification](https://kdl.dev/spec/)

The concealed raw body can then poison brace counting and reach the same silent-sibling-loss removal path above. `remove_vertex_kind` has no separate comment refusal.

**Fix direction:** detect zero-hash raw openers at a valid token boundary independently of quote state, or make the refusal scan comment-aware/conservatively refuse the relevant comment syntax before relying on quote tracking.

### Committed suite

Executed successfully with uv’s cache redirected because the sandbox denied access to `~/.cache/uv`:

```text
UV_CACHE_DIR=/private/tmp/loops-uv-cache uv run --package lang pytest libs/lang/tests
1791 collected
1710 passed
81 skipped
2.90s
```

The committed R5 additions and corpus round-trip oracle pass, but they do not cover either static evasion above.
